{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed graph stored as out- and in-adjacency lists."}],"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/MutableDirectedGraph","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s28CustomDebugStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s17CustomReflectableP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/Se","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/SE","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/SQ","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s30ExpressibleByDictionaryLiteralP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/SH","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"AdjacencyList","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The vertex set is any set of ","type":"text"},{"code":"Hashable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" values. The edge set is a set of ordered pairs of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertices: self-loops are allowed, parallel edges are not.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Vertices are kept in dense slots, with a dictionary from vertex to slot. Edges are kept in an","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"array, so an edge’s position in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"text":" is an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"text":" in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<edgeCount"},{"text":", and a weight can live","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in an array beside the graph. Each slot has a row of the slots of its out-neighbors, a parallel","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"row of those edges’ positions, and a row of its in-neighbors; the rows of each kind share one","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"array, so the graph makes a constant number of allocations however many vertices it has","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(amortized, like ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Array"},{"text":"), and copying it copies a constant number of buffers. A dictionary from","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"slot pair to position answers ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contains(edge:)"},{"text":" in O(1).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Removing an edge is O(1): the last edge moves into its position, and the last entry of each row","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"into the hole. Removing a vertex costs O(degree) and moves the last slot into its place. So","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex order, edge order and edge positions are unspecified and may change after a removal.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/adjacencylistmodule\/adjacencylist"]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\/documentation\/AdjacencyListModule\/AdjacencyList"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/AdjacencyListModule\